-- THE JOIN and THE DEADLINE as VALUES (EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §2.6 card
-- B1, built 2026-10-24) name a position in the life of the obligation whose
-- HENCE or LEST they are WRITTEN in, so written at the top level — in a
-- rule's body, in a top-level rule's WHERE, as a function's result — they
-- name nothing, and are refused as the bare anchor is (refusal 1 of
-- §5.1.1.1). THE ARMING is refused in those same places by its own rule
-- (refusal 8, card B1c; lifecycle-arming-outside-obligation.l4): the
-- machine binds it only in an obligation's own lines and under a HENCE or
-- LEST, so in a top-level obligation's own WITHIN it is that obligation's
-- arming (run-lifecycle-values.l4 pins it).

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Tenant HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Pay  HAS amount IS A NUMBER

alice MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"

GIVETH A NUMBER
`when it joined` MEANS THE JOIN PLUS 1

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`alias at the top` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 5 OF t
    WHERE t MEANS THE DEADLINE
